  "about": "One figure for one graph (decided 2026-10-07): the template listing at the 180-minute cap, the server's run estimate (estimateWorkflowCredits) and the editor's run estimate (estimateRunCreditLines) all quote these base totals while the preview stop rule (PREVIEW_STOP_RULE_ENABLED) is off. A graph whose render is set to Preview (the four podcast templates, decided 2026-10-08) is listed in two parts: `templates` is its preview part (the whole graph at its saved settings, the run estimate of a whole run with the rule off) and `templateFinals` its Render final (the render at Final and every node after it, the run estimate of that Render final). With the rule on, a run stops at the Preview and its estimate leaves out the nodes after the render: `templateRunsWithStopRule` is that run estimate, below the preview part by that tail; the listing and a whole-graph estimate still quote `templates`. The sync writes the four that way only where the rule is on (decided 2026-10-08); where it is off it writes their render at Final, and `templatesSyncedWithoutStopRule` is that graph's one figure: its listing (it has no Render final part), its run estimate and its whole-graph estimate. Read by backend/src/lib/tutorial-seed/__tests__/run-estimate-parity.test.ts and frontend/src/lib/__tests__/run-estimate-parity.test.ts.",
